WEBVTT

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:05.200
Assistant Inspector Shizumu
fired seven rounds.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.110
And the suspect fired
two hollow-point rounds.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.980
Were there any other shots fired?

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.680
We have no trace of anything else.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:18.220
<i>The suspect fired at
point-blank range and missed,</i>

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.870
...<i>yet Shizumu landed all of his shots...</i>

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.440
...<i>I have a funny feeling about this...</i>

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.120
Thank you for the other day.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:31.880
My boss told me that you filed the
paperwork to have my magic use approved.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.630
It was the right thing
to do in that situation.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.940
Still, it made me really happy.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.640
I've been causing a lot
...of trouble for my agency...

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:43.300
So, thank you very much!

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.960
You came all this way just to say that?

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.280
Yes, I wanted to thank you in person.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.500
...Oh, right...

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:53.520
...This isn't much, but...

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.400
What's this?

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.900
A protective stone tied
to the archangel Michael.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:02.100
Michael is the guardian angel
for paramedics and police officers.

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:03.530
Oh?

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.660
You're a police officer,
so I thought it'd be perfect for you.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:10.120
Thank you.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.170
So what's with the suitcase?
Going somewhere?

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.520
Oh, yes.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.590
I'm going to Boston, USA.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.420
Oh no! I'm going to
miss our meeting time!

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.480
Okay, I'm off!

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.010
All right. Take care.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:22.040
Thanks!

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.560
How could you make that mistake?

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:34.270
Is this your first time in Narita Airport?

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:39.340
But even <i>you were saying,
"It's no problem."</i>

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:41.940
Cecilcchi!

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:42.400
I-I'm sorry that I'm late!

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.950
Jeez. What were you doing?

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.950
We were waiting for you!

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.160
Good grief.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.160
What do you think would happen
if we'd missed our flight?

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.180
Looks like checking in
online was the right move.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:53.560
...Oh no, I forgot to bring soy sauce...

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.540
And the fried noodles and cabbage.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.160
What were you going to make?

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.280
The famous Nagasaki dish sara udon.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.500
I see, I guess we won't be
having much Japanese food now.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.980
I should have brought some nuka pickles too!

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.980
We're only going for five days and three nights.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:10.140
Well, the two of them have never been overseas,
so you'll have to keep an eye on them.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.960
...Take care and have a safe trip...

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.400
...Have a safe trip, Cecilun...

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:18.980
...O-Okay...

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:21.280
I won't forget about you, Moyoyon.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.440
Cecilun!

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.280
Stop crying, Moyoyon.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.720
Natcchi!

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:26.620
What?

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.300
Please take care of Cecilun!

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:33.020
...You're the only one I can count on...

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.480
Are you her mother?

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.360
Natcchi, do you fly often?

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:49.780
Well, I don't hate trips,

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:52.520
but for graduation,
I traveled around Europe.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.450
Europe, huh?

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:55.400
Where did you go?

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:59.780
England, France, Germany,
and Spain in a rental car.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.090
You drove yourself?

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:04.360
Yes, I have an international
driver's license.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.760
Wow.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.120
It's not that special.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.260
But you lived in Canada,
didn't you, Cecilcchi?

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.120
You should visit sometime.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.700
...I've always wanted to live abroad...

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:18.130
I hear Japanese girls get hit on all the time.

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.960
I'm sure they have standards, though.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.760
What're you saying, Hachimitsu?

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.920
Oh, Boston?

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:40.020
That sounds nice.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:44.150
It's a business trip, though,
so we'll be training.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.560
Apparently, the head
of Helsing Law Offices

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.820
and Ageha were friends in school.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:50.790
Oh.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:54.790
I wish I could go visit Dad too.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.280
I wanna tell him about you.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.780
Don't worry.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.800
Your father sends me letters,

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.970
and I've sent some back.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.330
We both know how the other's doing.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:06.800
Okay.

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:13.680
I've gotta find new evidence soon.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:23.980
I will carry my indomitable hope into the dark night

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:23.980
yami no naka no shinjitsu ga hikari kagayaku you ni

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:30.270
so that it may light a shining fire of truth there

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:30.270
kagi no nai kibou wo tokihanatou

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:45.720
I was born bleeding from my hands,

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:45.720
naze te no hira no kizu wo daite umareochita imi

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:49.710
and why was I born not a thousand years in the past or the future,

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:49.710
sennen kako demo mirai demo naku

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.010
but in the present?

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.010
erabareta ima

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:55.370
The scales of justice are fragile

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:55.370
zen'aku hakaru tenbin wa zeijaku

00:04:55.370 --> 00:05:00.430
The waning, waxing moon calls to a flower on the earth

00:04:55.370 --> 00:05:00.430
michikakeru tsuki ga izanau gisei no chi ni saita

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.330
the color of blood

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.330
chi no iro no hana

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.830
I will give all I have

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.830
tatta hitotsu kanau nara

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.490
if it means one of my wishes will come true

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.490
subete wo sasageyou

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.800
I have a "post nubila phoebus" kind of personality

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.800
post nubila phoebus kokoro

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.660
which I will show the world

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.660
kaze ni hanatte

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.660
I want to slash apart the curtain of raven black,

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.660
shikkoku no curtain hikichigiri

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.350
and look at a new world

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.350
chigau sora wo mitemitai

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:21.020
My love stabs at the cracks

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:21.020
sabita unmei no hibiware

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:23.490
of a stagnant fate

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:23.490
omoi wa nejikonde

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:26.350
No matter how long the storm lasts,

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:26.350
donnani arasoi tsuzuketemo

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.960
time itself will not stop breathing

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.960
toki wa kokyuu wo yamenai

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.720
What remains after destruction, rebirth,

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.720
kowashite tsunde kowashite

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:34.190
and further destruction?

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:34.190
nani ga nokoru darou

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:36.920
I'm sure I can put an end to a thousand nights of doubt

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:36.920
sou nanajuuokuban no mayoi mo

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:40.060
and to the system of the world

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:40.060
sono haichizu wa kakikaerareru

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.730
I'm sure that one day I will find a place where I can shine

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.730
moetsukitemo kagayakeru basho e

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:46.970
even if only ashes will remain

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:46.970
itsuka tadoritsukeru

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:54.000
Maple Leaf in CANADA

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:54.000
Case 7

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.130
We're finally in America!

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.380
This is my first time overseas!

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:04.760
Thank you for coming.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.950
I'm one of the associates, Diana.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:11.770
I'll be taking care of you
during your stay.

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:13.690
It's a pleasure to meet you all.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:16.070
Thank you for everything.

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:17.950
No, we should be thanking you.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.320
We'd like to use this opportunity

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.970
to understand the differences between
the Japanese and American Courts for Magic,

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:24.240
and to also get to
know each other better.

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:26.990
That's also what Kynt,
the head of our office, wants.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:27.660
Oh?

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:29.790
A checkpoint?

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.950
Hello.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.370
What happened?

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:41.380
There's a chance that the robbery-murder
suspect, Geah Grim, is nearby.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.130
Robbery and murder?

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:45.720
Yeah, this guy.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:48.590
He's a dangerous man.
Please be careful.

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:51.100
...This doesn't seem like a safe place...

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:53.770
I hope you won't get involved again.

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:56.030
Thanks for your concern.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:57.980
Dummy, he's being sarcastic.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:01.980
Nice to meet you.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:05.230
I am the head of
Helsing Law Offices, Kynt.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.240
Nice to meet you.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:11.470
I'm Chouno, a senior partner
at Butterfly Law Offices.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:13.470
You must be tired after your long trip.

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:17.030
Are you a wizard barrister too?

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:19.450
You look a bit young.

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:22.750
I'm only seventeen, but I'm a
wizard barrister at Butterfly Law Offices.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.390
Seventeen?

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:27.410
There aren't any wizard barristers
that young in America.

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:28.760
That's amazing.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:31.260
Th-Thank you.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.870
What's your name?

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:34.770
Sudou Cecil.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.550
We finished training pretty early,

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:07.950
so would you like to see
some of the sights in Boston?

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:10.130
If you want, I'll show you around.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.150
Wow, really?

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:13.040
All right!

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:13.890
This is what I was waiting for.

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:17.520
Cecil, you can go visit
...your home in Canada.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:19.270
Really?

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:20.220
Yes.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:23.800
Actually, Agehappi
said I should let you go.

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:25.310
Thank you very much!

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.530
Hooray!

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:30.780
Oh, but what should I do
...about the flight... and money...

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:32.780
Are you going by yourself?

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:36.150
What, are you lonely, Hachimitsu?

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:37.420
No.

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:40.410
Sudou tends to get easily
involved in strange incidents.

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:43.520
Oh, then I've got an idea.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:51.910
We'll just have her go by rental car,
and see that she isn't alone.

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:54.850
Oh, then please
feel free to use our car.

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:56.260
Are you sure that's all right?

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:58.960
Wait, why me?!

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:00.980
Don't decide something
like that for me!

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:03.210
You have an international
driver's license, right?

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:04.520
You're the perfect candidate.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:08.030
We're counting on you, Hotarin.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.780
Take care of Cecilcchi.

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:19.410
From Boston, it's 650 miles to Lake Huron.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:22.690
So it's an eleven-hour trip.

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:24.410
It's a lot closer than I thought.

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:28.910
...Um...

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:29.920
Don't talk to me.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.950
It distracts me while driving.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:36.690
And I have no reason to do this for you,

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:37.930
so you owe me one.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:39.890
...Right...

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.490
I'm hungry.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:45.250
You have snacks, don't you?

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.370
Just eat those.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:49.500
Why isn't the tank full?

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:00.750
Damn it, what the hell?

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.210
You can't use that here.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:06.730
You have to use their
corporate credit card here.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:18.590
I would always watch my dad
gas up the car when I was little.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:19.930
Are you trying to brag?

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:22.180
No, I wasn't!

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:25.240
All right. Hurry up and fill her up.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.060
...She's way too moody...

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.830
That's not being moody,
it's flat-out rude!

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:53.510
The engine stalled?

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:57.040
This is why you can't rely on machines.

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:59.510
Don't just sit there,
get out and help me push.

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:00.710
R-Right!

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.100
What is this?

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:06.480
What's wrong?

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:08.520
They haven't maintained the car at all!

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.600
It's unreal!

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:12.880
Um, if there's something
...I can help with—

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:13.770
Shut up!

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.900
You wouldn't know what to do,
so just keep your mouth shut!

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:18.850
Why are you yelling?

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:21.030
You're just taking it
out on me, Natcchi.

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:25.850
Taking it out on you?
Whose fault do you think this is?

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:28.540
I'm not your babysitter!

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:30.670
...I'm sorry...

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.420
I'm done with this.

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:57.070
Still not fixed?

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:59.030
Shut up, you perverted frog!

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:06.070
It started!

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:09.710
The battery connections
were just loose.

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:10.950
You're amazing, Natcchi.

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:12.750
I never knew you were this talented!

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:13.850
Of course.

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:16.590
You're so cool!
I want to say that one day too!

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:31.270
...S-Sorry...

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:35.150
I shouldn't be dozing off
while you're driving.

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:37.910
I'll get tired if we don't talk.

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:40.150
Let's just talk about
something, Natcchi.

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:43.150
Oh, am I distracting you?

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:45.170
Not really.

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:48.070
...I've been meaning to ask you...

00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:51.540
When did you come to Japan?

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:55.410
I used to come to Japan
...often when I was a kid, but...

00:12:56.020 --> 00:13:00.050
When I was eleven, Mom had to return
to her family home, so ever since then.

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:02.470
Because of your father's job?

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:04.050
No.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:08.060
I guess my mom wanted me
to go to a Japanese school.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:11.190
What about you, Natcchi?

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:13.530
What was it like for you growing up?

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.530
What was it like?

00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:17.490
Well, I was cheerful and energetic.

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:18.500
Huh?

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:19.570
What?

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:22.070
Nothing, it's just a bit unexpected.

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:28.570
People have to change
regardless if they want to or not.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.130
Y-You can do it, Natcchi!

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:34.040
I don't need you to cheer me on.

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:37.170
...<i>She's all moody again...</i>

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:42.730
Hey, Hotaru.

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:45.130
When will we reach Canada?

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:47.510
If you don't hurry, it'll get dark.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.010
You don't have to tell me.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:53.550
You've been driving all day,
so you must be tired, though.

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:55.020
We should camp out tonight.

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:57.530
Huh? Camp out in a foreign country?

00:13:57.530 --> 00:13:58.650
What's wrong with you?

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.590
But we don't have any money.

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:02.070
I <i>did borrow a tent, though.</i>

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:03.600
Why would we camp?!

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:04.720
I can't believe this!

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:05.750
I don't even understand!

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:07.080
How could you even suggest that?

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:07.100
L-Look out!

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.870
...You idiot... I almost ran them over!

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.730
Let's give them a ride.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:16.030
No way!

00:14:16.030 --> 00:14:17.970
What if they're a robber?

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:19.430
It's fine.

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:20.190
See?

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:21.790
Huh? Hey! Whoa!

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:24.630
It'd be mean to leave a girl here.

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:26.260
She's Japanese?

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:28.910
Besides, if all else fails,
we have magic.

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:37.910
Thank goodness you're
going in the same direction.

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.020
My name is Kaede.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.730
Are you sightseeing in Canada?

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:46.070
No, I'm studying here.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:47.610
I want to become a wizard barrister.

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:50.370
Is something wrong?

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:52.370
We're wizard barristers.

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:54.230
Huh? Really?

00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:55.450
...But...

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.120
Please call me Cecil.

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:00.120
I work as a wizard barrister
at the same agency as Natcchi.

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:03.230
She's the youngest
wizard barrister in history.

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:04.930
Wow, that's amazing!

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:08.970
Why did you become a
wizard barrister at such a young age?

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:09.970
Huh?

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:14.680
...Oh, I wanted to help people in need...

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:16.410
That's very admirable.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:18.180
I'll need to work hard too.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:24.190
I think the Court for Magic's
wrong for only holding one trial.

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:27.090
They say it's due to trial efficiency.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:30.700
But I think it's just because
they're prejudiced against Wuds.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:33.080
The judge is human too.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:34.930
I think that's just wrong.

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:38.200
Wuds are a minority,
so their voices may go unheard,

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:40.890
but if we can't talk with one another,

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:43.210
I don't think we can
coexist with humans.

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:45.420
What do you two think?

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:52.470
I think that humans and Wuds need to
accept the good and bad in each other.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:55.530
But it's not going to be easy.

00:15:57.460 --> 00:15:59.150
What about you, Cecil?

00:15:59.150 --> 00:16:01.850
I'd love for the prejudice
against Wuds to stop,

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:03.980
but I don't think that'll happen.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:07.730
I think that's why
wizard barristers are needed.

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:12.240
So they can be on the side of Wuds—
the people who face discrimination.

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:17.550
Huh?

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:20.080
You like <i>Lethal Vampire too, Hotaru?</i>

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.330
I love the horror-action genre.

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:25.650
Each movie is different,
so it never gets boring.

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:28.340
I know, right? I loved part four!

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:31.530
I think the best one was part five.

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.490
The writing was great in that one.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:36.410
Part six was like that too.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:38.030
What about you, Cecil?

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:41.510
...I haven't seen any movies in years...

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:41.970
What?

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:43.930
These are classics, though!

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:44.730
You don't know 'em?

00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:46.750
No.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:48.370
What sort of music are you into?

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:51.710
I don't really keep up with recent music,
but I do know some of the older songs.

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:53.450
C'mon, Cecil.

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:55.410
You've gotta keep up with the times!

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:56.490
Whoa, what?!

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:58.890
...Yeah...

00:16:58.890 --> 00:17:04.870
I was just so busy studying for the
bar exam that I shut out other information.

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.050
What?

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:08.000
When did you start studying?

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:09.450
When I was thirteen.

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:11.050
Thirteen? Seriously?

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:14.050
...I really wanted to pass, so...

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:24.310
Hey.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:25.230
Hm?

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:29.750
You said you started
studying for the bar at thirteen.

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:32.730
Why were you in such a hurry?

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.360
I'm going to look for some onions.

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:49.710
It's delicious!

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:51.470
What bliss.

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:53.970
I didn't know you were so
talented, you perverted frog.

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:57.960
This is nothing to The Great Nana Genie!

00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:01.270
This is probably decent,
even for me.

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:06.600
Cecil doesn't cook at all.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:08.980
...S-Slow down a bit...

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:12.150
Cecil, I won't say anything bad,

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:14.990
but you should really
start to practice cooking.

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:18.990
The key to a man's heart
is through his stomach.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:24.690
What?

00:18:24.690 --> 00:18:26.210
...Well...

00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:29.170
Natcchi, you just sounded like Sori!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:32.250
Do you have someone you like, Hotaru?

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.190
...N-Not really...

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:36.890
Is it someone from
Butterfly Law Offices?

00:18:36.890 --> 00:18:38.010
Oh?

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:40.010
So someone hot works there?

00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:43.010
Wh-What's wrong, Natcchi?!

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:49.270
Want more curry?

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:54.920
He's married.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:56.530
He was my professor.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:59.520
So you're having an affair?

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:01.450
...It hasn't gotten that far...

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:02.750
It's unrequited.

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:06.930
Every day after work,
I'd go to his lectures.

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:08.790
So that's why you always
...leave work at five...

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:12.590
I thought I didn't care
if he ever looked my way,

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:14.710
as long as I could keep loving him.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:17.770
...But I need to end it soon...

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:24.660
It's so pretty.

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:27.620
It's completely different
from the night sky in Tokyo.

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:29.810
I haven't seen this in a while.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:33.610
When I was little,
I would look up at it with my dad.

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:36.070
Does your dad live in Japan?

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:40.830
We've lived apart since before I started
studying overseas for certain reasons.

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:42.910
But even though I can't see him,

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:47.370
knowing that this sky's
connected to Japan's cheers me up.

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:50.330
You must really love your father.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:53.230
He raised me on his own.

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:57.330
No matter what others may think,
he's my precious family.

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.590
...You have to believe in your family...

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:06.370
I have to help my mom.

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:08.350
Tell us.

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.120
Huh?

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:12.850
I told you my story,
so now it's your turn.

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:16.860
You're hiding something, aren't you?

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:19.110
...Natcchi...

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:30.620
My mom's on death row.

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:33.010
Soon after we arrived in Japan,

00:20:33.010 --> 00:20:36.130
we were involved in an incident
which almost cost me my life.

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:40.210
My mom used magic and
killed the person attacking me.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:43.910
Even though we said
it was self-defense,

00:20:43.910 --> 00:20:47.500
the judge and police wouldn't listen,

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:49.370
due to their prejudice against Wuds.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:53.690
So I want to become a full-fledged
wizard barrister, so I can help my mom.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:56.670
...To request a retrial...

00:20:58.680 --> 00:21:00.010
So that's why.

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:06.610
Welcome to Canada!

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:08.830
Yay!

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:10.550
We're finally in Canada, Nana Genie!

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:13.870
Now that we've crossed
...the border, I'm hungry...

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:15.230
All right.

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:16.880
Let's go get some food.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.690
Thanks for the meal.

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:25.910
That was great.

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:29.290
...Hey, Cecil, so where are we going after...

00:21:31.610 --> 00:21:34.890
Hurry and hand over the money,
unless you want to die!

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:37.010
...The fugitive...

00:21:37.010 --> 00:21:38.060
Geah Grim!

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:39.140
...You're kidding...

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:41.190
Don't move!

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:42.170
...You're bleeding...

00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:44.320
I'm fine, it's just a graze.

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:50.050
...Damn it...

00:21:50.050 --> 00:21:51.280
A Wud!

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:03.290
Why?

00:22:03.290 --> 00:22:04.130
You're kidding.

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:06.870
...Never thought we'd meet...

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:09.050
...at a place like this, Cecil....

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:32.660
My heart may cry silently,

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:32.660
kokoro ga donna ni namida afuretemo

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:40.210
but I still want to behold the blue sky

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:40.210
hitomi ni aozora utsushiteitai

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:47.800
I want to have something like the strength of flowers

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:47.800
concrete-iro no machi no katasumi ni

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:55.220
which bloom in the nooks of the endless concrete of the city

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:55.220
sotto saku hana no tsuyosa wo manetai

00:22:55.220 --> 00:23:02.620
Starting today, I won't try to wriggle out by saying

00:22:55.220 --> 00:23:02.620
maegami ga jama de mienai nante iiwake

00:23:02.620 --> 00:23:06.440
that I saw nothing because my hair was in the way

00:23:02.620 --> 00:23:06.440
kyou kara shinai

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:14.930
Beyond the horizon, my future awaits me,

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:14.930
chiheisen no mukou ni ashita ga matteru kara

00:23:14.930 --> 00:23:20.160
so I will let the sun in my heart

00:23:14.930 --> 00:23:20.160
kono mune no hitotsu no taiyou

00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:22.210
shine out far and wide

00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:22.210
tooku hanatte

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:29.550
I will overtake the earth's rotation on the path I walk,

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:29.550
chikyuu no jiten wo oikosu kurai hitamuki ni arukou

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:37.680
with trusting love inside my heart

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:37.680
shinjiru omoi dakishimete doko made mo
